{"data":{"codec":"utf8","content_ref":"inline:The hypothesis that the Collatz conjecture is undecidable depends on the existence of a covering principle where the 3n+1 map is isomorphic to a Universal Turing Machine; this is refuted if a proof is constructed within ZFC or if the map's computational capacity is proven to be bounded below the threshold of Turing-completeness.","id":"aae99967831155231090375b92c4ff83385e8a9677c4f73f36362c56383204bf","interface":{"commitments":["hv-floor@2a45b7988522","lineage-ref@87e07fc0bd67","relation-form@578e42df713e"],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"01bf53c1c46db20ce0f85c7f4faa04bb92fe6303c875aa554ef2f630bc9ac7e2"},{"role":"dependence","target":"02c0b151a821336773cea16c575a8b20e961efd5eacfa8c8f47b6ad876ecf797"},{"role":"dependence","target":"1b80edf484c11458b42afdb9723f859acf25ed021882d109fc76b2eac62a35ce"},{"role":"dependence","target":"36f37fce12fd832574b46b7780c283940e479e57b89feae0db15a8f002f1b760"},{"role":"dependence","target":"cd36bf34d053d0b2e9958008575854e54d4f292714d84ed179160239545550ee"}]},"provenance":{"event_seq":597,"role":"conjecturer","school":"school-2"},"warrants":[]},"id":"aae99967831155231090375b92c4ff83385e8a9677c4f73f36362c56383204bf","schema":"artifact"}